Politically, modernity in China is characterized by the Communist Party's (CPC) continued dominance. Despite some liberalization, the CPC maintains tight control over political discourse and governance. There is a growing emphasis on the rule of law and individual rights, reflecting a nuanced approach to modern political values within a one-party system.

